**The fix:** commit bd636ad2 puts the exception on `cross-test/chaos/orchestrator/orchestrator.go:77`, as Jody decided:
`// #nosec G404 -- seeded on purpose: the report's seed replays the run (#571)`
- Nothing was added to `security-exceptions.yaml`.
- The generator code is unchanged, so the same profile seed still gives the same schedule.
- gosec now reports G404 in `cross-test/chaos` only at `fault/fault.go:125`, which is #570.
- `go test ./orchestrator/` passes.

**Land:** queued at 17:36Z and still waiting for its verdict at 21:15Z. The manager lands it after this run and posts the result on the issue.

**My `just gates` run:** 15 of the 16 legs passed. `current-generation` failed on four tests in the generated Go durable accounting spool (`accounting_sink_durable_test.go` lines 93, 120, 152 and 196). They wait about one second for records, and the gates and the land were running at the same time on a loaded machine. My change is one comment in `cross-test/chaos`, so I don't think it caused this, but I haven't confirmed it. I re-ran `current-generation` alone; it hadn't reached those tests by the time limit, and I stopped it. Rule 7 says the release needs the full gates passing, so this still has to be settled.

**Patch releases:** main has taken features since v2.6.1 (for example #321), so no patch is cut from main. Every release line has the same line, so I opened backport PRs. Each one passes its local test and is clean in gosec, but I did not run `just gates` on any of them.

